* The second queue manager of the IBM MQ suite: the far end of a sender/receiver channel pair.
* It owns the queues the first queue manager writes to through a remote queue definition and an
* administrative subscription, and it requires a client certificate on the channel (mutual TLS).

* The queue manager's certificate and its CA, in a PKCS#12 key repository (see qm1.mqsc).
ALTER QMGR SSLKEYR('/sutra-tls/qm.p12') KEYRPWD('@KEYRPWD@') CERTLABL('qm')
REFRESH SECURITY TYPE(SSL)
DEFINE QLOCAL('QM2.IN') REPLACE
DEFINE QLOCAL('QM2.NOTIFY') REPLACE
DEFINE CHANNEL('QM1.TO.QM2') CHLTYPE(RCVR) TRPTYPE(TCP) +
       SSLCIPH('ANY_TLS12_OR_HIGHER') SSLCAUTH(REQUIRED) REPLACE
* The developer configuration blocks every channel by default; let the receiver in.
SET CHLAUTH('QM1.TO.QM2') TYPE(ADDRESSMAP) ADDRESS('*') USERSRC(CHANNEL) ACTION(REPLACE)
SET CHLAUTH('QM1.TO.QM2') TYPE(BLOCKUSER) USERLIST('nobody') ACTION(REPLACE)
